  "interpretation": [
    "The seed-20261023 failure is a ranking failure on both consumed 337.1-Hz phase cases: correct grouped candidates and frozen voiced decisions remain available.",
    "The wrong one-third-frequency candidate combines AMDF and suffix-window correlation evidence; correct candidates are separate acceptable groups. Passing seeds show the architecture can represent a correct ranking.",
    "At the saved failing center frames, total acceptable softmax mass exceeds the winning alias probability, although each individual acceptable candidate loses. Set CE still penalizes alias mass; the proposed max-good hinge aligns more directly with the emitted argmax.",
    "For tanh of a linear neighbor-plus-relative-log-frequency message, the query-dependent ratio term is constant across neighbors. Monotonic tanh allows it outside the neighbor max, so winning neighbor/channel is query-independent absent floating ties. The final shared scorer can still make query-dependent decisions.",
    "Removing only the relative-ratio input from frozen weights is diagnostic, not a trained comparator: seed22 continues passing, seed23 continues failing, and seed24 fails. This does not prove that a ratio-free trained architecture cannot solve the task.",
    "Alias-specific and all-negative margin objectives change both negative eligibility and eligible-row averaging. Any improvement is not an isolated effect of harmonic knowledge.",
    "Only 517 grouped-covered training frames have reference F0 at least 300 Hz, across four dependent observation conditions; 126 contain a one-third alias. The experiment cannot establish broad physical support coverage.",
    "Factor counts overlap across anchors and factors. Rows, negative candidates and acceptable-negative pairs are separate denominators.",
    "All waveforms and challenge outcomes used here were already consumed. No new validation outcome, fit, threshold choice, calibrated confidence or deployment qualification is claimed."
  ]
